            //   This is: PUSH2(n+1) PUSH1(0x00) CODECOPY RETURNDATASIZE RETURN
            //   CODECOPY copies n+1 bytes from code offset (init_code_size) to memory offset 0
            //   Then RETURN returns memory[0..n+1] = init_code ++ data... no that's wrong.

            // Actually the standard SSTORE2:
            // We store init code before the data in memory.
            // init code = 0x61 ++ (n+1) ++ 0x60 ++ 0x00 ++ 0x39 ++ 0x3d ++ 0xf3 (7 bytes)
            // This does: CODECOPY(0, 7, n+1) then RETURN(0, n+1)
            // Wait no, CODECOPY(destOffset, offset, size)
